# Portfolio Deployment

## Frontend — GitHub Pages

- **Base path**: `/Portfolio_Website/` (set in `vite.config.js` and `BrowserRouter basename`)
- **CI**: `.github/workflows/deploy-frontend.yml` builds and deploys to `gh-pages`
- **Env**: Set `VITE_API_BASE_URL` to the production API URL at build time
- **Favicon**: `frontend/public/favicon.svg` — referenced in `index.html` with base path prefix

## Backend — Render (recommended) or Azure

1. Deploy `backend/` as a Web Service (.NET 8)
2. Set environment variables:
   - `DATABASE_URL` — PostgreSQL connection string
   - `JWT_SECRET` — min 32 characters
   - `ADMIN_USERNAME`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD` or `ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH`
   - `CORS_ORIGIN` — `https://<username>.github.io` (comma-separate multiple origins)
   - `SENDGRID_API_KEY` or email provider key
3. Health check path: `/health`

## CORS

Backend `Cors:Origins` must include the GitHub Pages origin exactly (no trailing slash on origin).

## LinkedIn UTM tracking

Share URL: `https://<username>.github.io/Portfolio_Website/?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=social`

## Post-deploy checklist

- [ ] `/health` returns 200 on Render
- [ ] Contact form sends email (or logs in dev)
- [ ] Analytics visits appear in admin dashboard with real geo in production
- [ ] GitHub Pages site loads assets under `/Portfolio_Website/`
